  "title": "Checkerboard m-sequence-based c-VEP dataset from",
  "description": "A checkerboard-stimulus, m-sequence-based code-modulated visual evoked potential (c-VEP) EEG dataset from 16 healthy participants. It was collected to evaluate how the spatial frequency of visual stimuli affects the performance and user experience of c-VEP brain-computer interfaces. Each stimulus condition is stored as a separate session with three runs (two for training, one for testing), recorded with 16 EEG channels at 256 Hz.",
  "methods_description": "EEG was recorded from 16 channels at 256 Hz (standard_1005 montage, 50 Hz line frequency) while participants viewed binary m-sequence-modulated checkerboard stimuli. Each condition was recorded as a separate session, and each session had three runs (two for training, one for testing). The data were converted to BIDS using MOABB.",
